# Force LF line endings for shell scripts regardless of the checking-out
# platform's line-ending config (Windows checkouts otherwise convert LF ->
# CRLF via core.autocrlf, which breaks bash execution -- a CRLF shebang
# line fails as "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and CRLF anywhere else in
# the script can corrupt commands silently). No .sh files are tracked in
# this repo as of this change; this is a forward-looking policy so any
# script added later is never checked out with the wrong line endings.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
